    "description": "Remove the Actions access setting step, because the repo is public\n\n## Summary\n\nThis repo is now public, so a consumer repo no longer needs the Actions access setting. That setting applies only to a private repo. This PR removes the setup step from the README and corrects the design doc.\n\nThe design doc said that a public repo changes nothing. That is wrong. A public consumer repo can call a workflow only from a public repo. `jerridan/crew` is public, and its first run failed with \"workflow file issue\" while this repo was private.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `README.md`: removes the section \"The Actions access setting\" and its `gh api` command. The \"Set up CI\" intro now says that any repo can call the workflow and the action.\n- `docs/design/high-level-design.md`: replaces the access-setting paragraph with the public-repo rule.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `jerridan/crew` PR #101 calls `review.yml@v1` with no access setting. After the visibility change, its run passed every step and posted a review.\n- No link in the repo points at the removed anchor (`git grep actions-access-setting` finds nothing).\n- This change has no code, so it needs no test.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01R5KTT34ZNxeaL3HX8DoDSe\n",
